es an 'empty' flag would behave differently from one that reads `self.items`. The current implementation reads `self.items`, so it would be correct.","evidence":[{"kind":"file","ref":"src/pricing/cart.py","quote":"def is_empty(self) -> bool:"}],"spec_gap":true,"suggested_fix":"If Cart supports removing items, add a scenario that removes the last item and expects the cart to be empty."}],"riskiest_assumptions":["`Cart.items` is a list or other sequence that `Cart()` starts empty and that `add()` appends to, so `not self.items` reflects how many line items the cart holds. The diff does not show its definition.","The gate report's per-test results come from the committed head that contains the `is_empty` implementation, not from the earlier red commit described in the implementer's note.","Q-001 (method vs property) was settled as a method in call form, which the spec text `Cart.is_empty()` and the existing `subtotal()` convention support. A property would break the call form the criteria use."]}
